/-!
# Stabilizer-chain certificates

Verified data for the cardinality route with base `23, 22, 0, 1, 2, 5, 3`:

* the orbit of `23` has size `24` (BFS words over `m24c`, `m24d`);
* the stabilizer of `23` has orbit size `23` on `22` (powers of the
  23-cycle `m24c`);
* the next four levels have orbit sizes `22, 21, 20` and then `16` outside
  the block `B0 = {0,1,2,3,4,21,22,23}` (which the stabilizer of
  `23,22,0,1,2` preserves);
* the stabilizer of `23,22,0,1,2,5` moves `3` through the 3 points
  `{3,4,21} = B0 \ {0,1,2,22,23}`;
* the stabilizer of `23,22,0,1,2,5,3` is trivial (`FinalStabilizer.lean`).

The words below level 1 are the `M23` stabilizer-chain words reused
verbatim (which below their own first level are the `M22` words): the
generators `m24a`, `m24b`, `m24c` act on `0,…,22` exactly as `m23a`,
`m23b`, `m23c` do and fix the new point `23`.

No external computation is trusted here until it is represented as data and
checked by Lean.
-/

